<title>UK: British Aerospace down on competition worries.</title>
<headline>British Aerospace down on competition worries.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British Aerospace Plc fell on Tuesday as investors continued to fret about reports that BAe could lose out on a defence contract with Saudi Arabia to U.S. group Lockheed Martin Corp., traders said.</p>
<p>Shares in BAe were down 12p at 12.47-1/2 stg by 0955 GMT with volume at 909,968.</p>
<p>Press reports last Thursday said Saudi Arabia was considering buying 100 F-16 fighter jets manufactured by Lockheed rather than BAe's Tornado aircraft.</p>
<p>The company's share price has shed more than 40 points from 12.87 stg on Thursday after the reports.</p>
<p>-- Paul Carrel, London newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
